# Inventory Management System — Cursor Rules
# PHP + XAMPP | Multi-Department | Role-Based Access

## PROJECT OVERVIEW
This is a multi-department inventory management system built with PHP and XAMPP (Apache + MySQL).
It is NOT a framework-based app — pure PHP with sessions, no Laravel, no Symfony.

## TECH STACK
- Backend: PHP 8.x (procedural or light OOP)
- Database: MySQL via phpMyAdmin (XAMPP)
- Frontend: HTML, CSS, vanilla JavaScript (no React, no Vue)
- Excel export: PhpSpreadsheet via Composer
- Auth: PHP sessions + bcrypt password hashing
- Data tables: DataTables.js (sortable, filterable)

## FOLDER STRUCTURE CONVENTION
/project-root
  /auth         → login.php, logout.php, session middleware
  /exec         → Executive pages
  /prodmgr      → Production Manager pages
  /dept         → Shared dept pages (honey, paragis, cacao, csr)
  /pos          → POS walk-in sales (PIN-only access)
  /includes     → Shared PHP: db.php, auth_check.php, header.php, footer.php
  /assets       → CSS, JS, images
  /exports      → PhpSpreadsheet Excel export scripts

## AUTHENTICATION RULES
- Every page MUST call requireRole(['role1','role2']) at the top before any output
- Two completely separate session types:
  - $_SESSION['user_id'], $_SESSION['role'], $_SESSION['dept_id'] → regular users
  - $_SESSION['pos_authenticated'] → POS PIN only
- A POS PIN session MUST NEVER access inventory pages
- Passwords hashed with password_hash($pass, PASSWORD_BCRYPT)
- On login, route to homepage by role:
  - executive    → /exec/dashboard.php
  - prod_manager → /prodmgr/dashboard.php
  - tl           → /dept/home.php
  - staff        → /dept/home.php
  - pos          → /pos/index.php

## ROLE HIERARCHY (highest to lowest)
1. executive
2. prod_manager
3. tl (team leader)
4. staff
5. pos (PIN-only, separate session, not in hierarchy)

NOTE: There is NO manager role. It has been removed.
TL handles department-level input and beginning inventory.
Executive handles all approvals, corrections, and AR credit payments.

## DEPARTMENT SCOPING RULE
- Staff and TL queries MUST always include: WHERE dept_id = $_SESSION['dept_id']
- prod_manager and executive queries have NO dept_id filter (they see all)
- dept_id values: honey | paragis | cacao_brc | csr

## DATABASE TABLES

### Users & Auth
- roles: id, name, created_at
  -- role name values: executive | prod_manager | tl | staff | pos
- departments: id, name, created_at
  -- dept name values: honey | paragis | cacao_brc | csr
- users: id, name, email, password_hash, role_id, dept_id, is_active, created_at, updated_at
- pos_pins: id, pin_hash, label, is_active, created_at

### Inventory
- stocks: id, name, dept_id, unit, current_price, supplier_name, supplier_code, created_by, created_at
- stock_entries: id, stock_id, dept_id, qty, batching_date, supplier_batch_no, entered_by, created_at
- stock_deductions: id, stock_id, dept_id, qty, reason, deducted_by, created_at
- daily_stock_counts: id, stock_id, dept_id, qty_remaining, counted_by, count_date
- beginning_inventory: id, dept_id, stock_id, qty, set_by, month_year, created_at
- edit_requests: id, table_name, record_id, field_name, old_value, new_value, reason, requested_by, status (pending/approved/rejected), rejection_note, reviewed_by, reviewed_at, created_at
  -- rejection_note: required when status = 'rejected', nullable otherwise
  -- reviewed_by: FK to users (executive only)

### Products & Costing
- products: id, name, dept_id, size, variant, selling_price, baseline_cost, created_by, created_at
- product_formula: id, product_id, stock_id, qty_per_unit, price_at_creation, created_at
- stock_price_history: id, stock_id, old_price, new_price, changed_by, changed_at
- product_cost_history: id, product_id, old_cost, new_cost, triggered_by_stock_id, recalculated_at

### RTS
- rts_records: id, product_type, size, variant, qty, notes, recorded_by, record_date, created_at
- rts_reuse_log: id, product_type, size, variant, qty_reused, reused_by, reuse_date, created_at

### POS & AR
- pos_sales: id, product_id, qty, unit_price, total, buyer_name, buyer_credentials, sold_by_pin, sale_date, created_at
- pos_receipt_items: id, sale_id, product_id, qty, unit_price, line_total
- ar_credits: id, user_id, product_id, qty, price_at_time, total_amount, status (outstanding/paid), taken_at, paid_at, marked_paid_by, created_at
  -- marked_paid_by: FK to users, executive only

## FIELD VISIBILITY BY ROLE (stock input form)
- stock name, qty, batching_date: staff, tl, prod_manager, executive
- supplier_batch_no: prod_manager, executive only
- supplier_name, supplier_code: executive only
- price: executive only

## STAFF vs TL VISIBILITY (same table, different WHERE)
- staff: SELECT * FROM stock_entries WHERE entered_by = $_SESSION['user_id'] AND dept_id = $_SESSION['dept_id']
- tl:    SELECT * FROM stock_entries WHERE dept_id = $_SESSION['dept_id']

## EDIT REQUEST & CORRECTION FLOW
- WHO CAN SUBMIT: staff AND tl (both roles)
- WHO REVIEWS: executive ONLY — prod_manager cannot approve or reject
- Flow:
  1. Staff or TL submits to edit_requests with status = 'pending'
  2. Executive sees notification badge (COUNT WHERE status = 'pending')
  3. Executive approves → update original record, set status = 'approved', log reviewed_by + reviewed_at
  4. Executive rejects → set status = 'rejected', reviewed_by + reviewed_at + rejection_note (REQUIRED — must explain why)
  5. Original record is READ-ONLY while status = 'pending'
  6. Requester can see the outcome and rejection note on their requests page
- NEVER allow prod_manager to touch edit_requests approval — executive only

## BEGINNING INVENTORY
- Set by: TL (for their own department only)
- Viewed by: TL (own dept), prod_manager (all depts), executive (all depts)
- Frequency: monthly, stored with month_year field

## EXCEL EXPORT ACCESS
- prod_manager: can export all dept reports
- executive: can export everything including pricing reports
- tl: NO export access
- staff: NO export access

## PRODUCT COSTING LOGIC
- baseline cost = sum of (price_at_creation × qty_per_unit) from product_formula at time of creation
- current cost  = sum of (stocks.current_price × product_formula.qty_per_unit)
- When executive updates a stock price:
  1. Save old price to stock_price_history
  2. Loop through all product_formula rows using that stock_id
  3. Recalculate each product's total cost
  4. Compare to last row in product_cost_history
  5. If changed: INSERT new row into product_cost_history
  6. All of steps 1-5 inside one PHP transaction
- Display: green badge if current < baseline, red badge if current > baseline

## RTS BALANCE QUERY
SELECT product_type, size, variant,
  COALESCE(SUM(r.qty),0) - COALESCE(SUM(u.qty_reused),0) AS balance
FROM rts_records r
LEFT JOIN rts_reuse_log u USING (product_type, size, variant)
GROUP BY product_type, size, variant

## RTS ACCESS RULES
- csr staff:    INSERT only, no SELECT of others' rows
- csr tl:       SELECT all rts_records + running totals
- prod_manager: SELECT all + can INSERT to rts_reuse_log
- executive:    SELECT all (read-only)
- all other roles: NO access to rts tables

## AR CREDIT RULES
- Triggered when any user takes a product: INSERT ar_credits with status = 'outstanding'
- This INSERT must be in the same transaction as the stock deduction
- Mark as paid: executive ONLY — UPDATE ar_credits SET status='paid', paid_at=NOW(), marked_paid_by=executive_id
- staff:        SELECT WHERE user_id = own id (own credits only)
- tl:           SELECT WHERE user_id = own id (own credits only)
- prod_manager: SELECT WHERE user_id = own id (own credits only)
- executive:    SELECT all credits across all users and departments + can mark as paid

## POS RULES
- Accessed via separate PIN (pos_pins table)
- Uses $_SESSION['pos_authenticated'] only
- Can SELECT products and selling_price
- On sale: INSERT pos_sales + pos_receipt_items + deduct from finished product stock
- Cannot access any page outside /pos/

## HONEY PRODUCT SPECIAL FIELDS
- size:    enum('liter','350ml','250ml','gallon')
- variant: enum('light','amber','dark')
- Both fields nullable — only required for honey products
- All forms involving honey must show/hide size+variant with JS based on product_type selection

## REPORTS ACCESS
- Daily/weekly/monthly dept report: tl (own dept, no export), prod_manager (all depts + export), executive (all depts + export)
- Cross-department report: prod_manager + executive only
- Pricing columns: executive only
- Beginning inventory: tl sets (own dept), prod_manager + executive view all

## EXCEL EXPORT
- Use PhpSpreadsheet (not PHPExcel — deprecated)
- Export must respect the same filters/WHERE clauses as the current table view
- Access: prod_manager and executive only

## CODE CONVENTIONS
- Use PDO with prepared statements — never raw mysqli string queries
- Always use transactions for any operation that writes to 2+ tables
- requireRole() must be the first function call on every protected page
- Never echo supplier_name, supplier_code, or price fields without checking role first
- Use consistent naming: snake_case for DB columns, camelCase for PHP variables
- All dates stored as DATETIME in MySQL, displayed formatted in PHP

## BUILD ORDER (do not skip phases)
Phase 1: roles, departments, users, login, session middleware, requireRole()
Phase 2: stocks, stock_entries, field visibility, DataTables, edit_requests + executive approval with rejection note
Phase 3: products, product_formula, stock_deductions, beginning_inventory (TL input)
Phase 4: stock_price_history, product_cost_history, costing recalculation loop
Phase 5: daily_stock_counts, reports (daily/weekly/monthly), Excel exports (prod_manager + exec only)
Phase 6: rts_records, rts_reuse_log, RTS pages, balance query
Phase 7: pos_pins, pos_sales, pos_receipt_items, POS UI
Phase 8: ar_credits, AR pages, executive mark-as-paid flow
